:::


<br>

## Get top 3 scores

Suppose you want to get the three students with the highest scores without sorting the data first. How can you do it? Polars has the method `top_k`, which you can use to accomplish exactly that.

::: {#eb141482 .cell execution_count=2}
``` {.python .cell-code}
(df
 .top_k(3, by='Score')
 )
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}
```{=html}
<div><style>
.dataframe > thead > tr,
.dataframe > tbody > tr {
  text-align: right;
  white-space: pre-wrap;
}
</style>
<small>shape: (3, 2)</small><table border="1" class="dataframe"><thead><tr><th>Student</th><th>Score</th></tr><tr><td>str</td><td>i64</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>&quot;Mike&quot;</td><td>93</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;Louis&quot;</td><td>91</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;Harvey&quot;</td><td>88</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
```
:::
:::


::: {.callout-tip}
If you want to get the bottom 3 students, use `bottom_k`.
:::

